1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:10,397
Speaking, task one. Topic 8: The Czech language. Ten questions. Listen to the question and answer aloud.

2
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:12,741
How long have you been learning Czech?

3
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:19,943
I've been learning Czech for about two years.

4
00:00:20,833 --> 00:00:22,302
How did you learn Czech?

5
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,267
I learned on a course, from an app on my phone and from TV.

6
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,900
Where do you speak Czech most often?

7
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:41,962
I speak Czech most often at work and in shops.

8
00:00:42,867 --> 00:00:44,511
Is Czech difficult for you?

9
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,179
Czech is difficult, especially the grammar and the pronunciation of ř.

10
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:55,965
What is the hardest thing in Czech for you?

11
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:04,511
The hardest for me are the cases and long vowels.

12
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:06,695
Do you read in Czech?

13
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:15,993
Yes, I read news online and sometimes short children's books.

14
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:18,644
Do you watch Czech TV?

15
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:27,293
Yes, in the evening I watch Czech news and series.

16
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,596
Why are you learning Czech?

17
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,964
I'm learning Czech because I live here and want permanent residence.

18
00:01:39,867 --> 00:01:41,462
How will you keep learning?

19
00:01:46,867 --> 00:01:49,758
I'll go to a course and talk more with Czech colleagues.

20
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:53,395
What would you advise someone who is starting Czech?

21
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,530
I'd advise them to speak every day, even if they make mistakes.

22
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:12,735
Great! Practise topic 8 on the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website, the link is in the video description. And subscribe — a new video every day.
